  "claim_boundary": "This v2 A0 package supersedes the unpublished v1 request because v1 left receipt and admission implementation choices open. It freezes the exact source-opportunity commitments together with the identity-free raw-transcript verifier, fixed anonymous observer, schemas, golden vectors, acquisition sequence, strict sole-first-revision Git object graph, two-pass equality rule, and fail-closed authority truth table before any target Gist exists. Request preparation itself performs no publication, anonymous target observation, Git fetch, source materialization, model execution, CUDA execution, or causal experiment. A future GO admission may establish only that a cooperatively executed pinned local observer reported the exact request bytes anonymously readable from one public Gist at two fresh observation passes and that pure byte replay found its API, returned raw bytes, public HTML presentation, sole advertised head, zero-parent commit, one-entry tree, exact three-object inventory, and blob transcripts self-consistent as one object graph. The stored HTTP and Git transcripts have no GitHub signature or transferable TLS proof; backend_kind, PID, nonce, command and environment ledgers can be forged by a malicious artifact producer, so third-party strong confirmation requires its own fresh reobservation or separate trusted attestation. It cannot establish continuous availability, WORM storage, trusted time, publisher or producer identity, resistance to a malicious local administrator, source outcomes, model outcomes, CUDA outcomes, or any Appendable, Readable, Learnable, Steerable, or integrated four-axis conclusion. Even GO authorizes only construction of the separately frozen A1 materializer contract and implementation; structural materialization and every experimental authority remain false until A1."
